---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import PageHeader from "../components/PageHeader.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Practice"
  description="Training and engagement for diplomats, mediators, and institutions working where generic values language fails."
>
  <PageHeader
    kicker="Training and engagement"
    title="Practice is a hearing, not a script."
    lede="CAV’s practice work is a stub by design. We will not ship a module that teaches people to pronounce a virtue they have not studied."
  />

  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5 py-12 sm:px-8">
    <article class="measure prose-cav text-[1.05rem]">
      <h2>Who this is for</h2>
      <p>
        Diplomats, mediators, humanitarian staff, institutional leaders, and teachers
        who already know that “shared values” sometimes ends a conversation that needed
        to continue.
      </p>

      <h2>What engagement will look like</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Briefings.</strong> Short, sourced sessions on a single concept and
          the harm of its usual English stand-in.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Seminars.</strong> Longer work on listening for remainder — the part
          of a moral claim that does not fit the talking points.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Institutional reviews.</strong> Reading a mission statement, code of
          conduct, or training deck for flattening language, and proposing sharper
          alternatives only where we have standing to do so.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Field methods.</strong> Practical habits: how to ask, how to wait,
          how to record a term without extracting it.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What we will not do</h2>
      <p>
        We will not certify cultural competence, sell a national-character profile, or
        train anyone to perform a virtue that is not theirs. Practice follows research.
        If an entry is still illustrative, the training is not for sale.
      </p>
      <p>
        Organizations that want to think with us while the curriculum is being written
        should start on the <a href="/join">Join</a> page.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
